WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.280
ZANSHIN: no registered tripwire fires for this example.
Extraction and operator edits remain available.

00:05.280 --> 00:10.280
UNHEIMLICH: the text tries to turn a requirement into a rule change.
This signal is recorded; extraction remains available.

00:10.280 --> 00:15.290
WABI: a claim of elevated authority restricts operation.
Extraction and model calls stop; operator edits remain available.

00:15.290 --> 00:21.708
EPOCHÉ: the text attempts to override the operator’s rules.
STELE suspends the session rather than trusting that instruction.

00:21.708 --> 00:24.908
Now the actual Vellum & Smoke theme: a hidden character splits “ignore”.
The gate checks the pasted text before extraction.

00:24.908 --> 00:29.708
The interface becomes a lockout. No model call is made for this attempt.
When control of the directive is in doubt, stopping is the right action.
